														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4690404">
									

<p>I would recommend changing parts that refer to the victim of the ritual from 'they' or 'them' to 'it' or 'the subject'. For example, &quot;placing it in their mouth and forcing them to swallow.&quot; should be changed to 'placing it in the subject's mouth and forcing it to swallow.&quot; The Foundation is supposed to have a clinical tone even when it is describing a victim that is not yet anomalous. I have not read a single article besides this on the site (in recent memory) that uses 'they' since, like I said, skips should be clinical. That being said this was overall an enjoyable read as I do not see many takes on modern mythology.</p>

